# No “demo” language in the product

This is a client-facing ride-hailing app (**Vuum**). Treat every screen as a real product.

## Never

- Put “demo”, “Demo”, “(demo)”, “for demo”, or “placeholder” in **user-visible** UI strings (buttons, titles, empty states, alerts).
- Explain mock/simulated behavior to the end user in the app.

## OK

- Internal code comments, docs, and Codemagic notes may mention mock/local data.
- Non-functional controls (e.g. Continue with Google) simply do nothing — no toast that says “demo only”.
